# ArrestDelta — environment
#
# The default build needs NOTHING here. The Supabase project this app used has
# been deleted, so the app ships in portfolio mode and serves every read and
# write from an in-browser emulation (`src/lib/localBackend`).
#
#   npm install && npm run dev
#
# The variables below only matter if you stand a real backend back up.

# Set to `live` to use a genuine Supabase project instead of the emulation.
# Anything else (or unset) keeps portfolio mode.
# VITE_APP_MODE=live

# Required when VITE_APP_MODE=live. Never commit real values.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# Portal data source: `demo` (in-memory simulator, default) or `live`.
# VITE_PORTAL_MODE=demo
